<section class="academic-section research-motivation" id="research-motivation">
<div class="section-copy"><h2>Why Mind, Act, and Coupling?</h2></div>
<div class="motivation-grid">
<article><span class="concept-name">Mind</span><h3>Memory and planning</h3><p>Retain task information, infer the required goal, and select the next operation.</p><div class="concept-scene"><b>Order → Goal</b></div></article>
<article><span class="concept-name">Act</span><h3>Physical execution</h3><p>Control contact, placement, and release so that an intended operation changes the physical scene.</p><div class="concept-scene"><b>Action → Outcome</b></div></article>
<article><span class="concept-name">Coupling</span><h3>Feedback and replanning</h3><p>Track what was actually completed and revise the remaining plan after a missed grasp or placement.</p><div class="concept-scene"><b>Outcome → Revised goal</b></div></article>
</div>
